\subsection{Phase 5: Multi-Attribute Radar Trade-Off and Pareto Analysis}
Figure~\ref{fig:radar} synthesizes algorithmic trade-offs across 5 normalized dimensions: Nominal Accuracy, Aging Robustness, Thermal Robustness, Convergence Speed, and Computational Efficiency. 

The radar plot highlights that no single classical algorithm dominates across all attributes. While EKF excels in computational simplicity and nominal fresh-cell accuracy, it collapses under aging. DEKF demonstrates the most balanced overall profile, trading a modest increase in computational overhead for comprehensive immunity against thermal and degradation variations.

